// What a Khayyam-written compiler needs fifth: a behaviour as a value. A reader
// hands each declaration it read to whoever asked for it, and an emitter hands
// each declaration back a body to compile; a library that takes a behaviour — a
// visitor, a reducer, a fold — is the ordinary shape of that.
//
// The language's position: a method's influencing group may receive a `vr`, an
// `sc`, or an `mt` (docs/khayyam/method.md → Type-level arguments for `sc` and
// `mt`), so a method is a legal argument; nothing states how a name writes one.

tp Text cp {
}

tp Emit mt (self Text) (body Method) () {
    body.Run()()
}

tp Run mt (self Text) () () {
    self.Print()()
}
